From 12c2b52a05781652ba38e62450c2f46aece9d062 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:33:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 354/371] pirates: a Black Pearl fort brought to 0 hp no longer
 closes the game; the fort gets a game state machine whose Death suits a fort
 (client patch 52, code only, no DC change, no restart)

Boats' BPFORT12 (16:21): real ship cannonballs took fort 401046696 from 5000 to 500 hp (7 hits) and the next hit took
it to 0. DistributedBattleAvatarAI.setHp sent setGameState('Death'), and every client near the fort closed with
BattleAvatarGameFSM.enterDeath -> motionFSM.off -> MotionFSM.enterOff, AttributeError 'MotionFSM' object has no
attribute 'animInfo': a fort has no getAnimInfo (its MotionFSM never got walk animations), and the avatar death path
after it would also need getEnterDeathTrack, which a fort lacks. Now DistributedFort.createGameFSM makes a FortGameFSM
(BattleAvatarGameFSM with its own enterDeath / exitDeath): Death only fades the local target tray if it shows this
fort, and does not respawn on exit. The fort's fall is still shown by died() from setHp (debris), and gameFSM.state
is 'Death' so TargetManager and WeaponBaseBase pass the dead fort by. Sim sim_fort_death.py (the real
BattleAvatarGameFSM and MotionFSM imported from the client tree; createGameFSM and FortGameFSM compiled out of the
file under test): live tree 2 of 2 cases close the game at MotionFSM.py line 580 (the BPFORT12 error), this tree 2 of
2 PASS; sim_fort_hp.py (0436) still 4 of 4 PASS on this tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 pirates/world/DistributedFort.py | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pirates/world/DistributedFort.py b/pirates/world/DistributedFort.py
index 3a5c259..ec70c70 100755
--- a/pirates/world/DistributedFort.py
+++ b/pirates/world/DistributedFort.py
@@ -19,6 +19,19 @@ from direct.interval.IntervalGlobal import *
 from pirates.effects import TextEffect
 from otp.otpbase import OTPRender
 
+
+class FortGameFSM(BattleAvatarGameFSM.BattleAvatarGameFSM):
+    # A fort at 0 hp is sent 'Death' (DistributedBattleAvatarAI.setHp). The avatar death path stops walk animations
+    # and plays a death animation, and a fort has neither: it closed the game for everyone near the fort (BPFORT12).
+    # The fort's fall is shown by died() from setHp; here it only becomes 'Death' so targeting passes it by.
+    def enterDeath(self, extraArgs = []):
+        tray = base.localAvatar.guiMgr.targetStatusTray
+        if tray.doId == self.av.getDoId():
+            tray.fadeOut()
+
+    def exitDeath(self):
+        pass
+
 class DistributedFort(DistributedBattleAvatar.DistributedBattleAvatar):
     notify = directNotify.newCategory('DistributedFort')
     endingR = 60
@@ -75,7 +88,7 @@ class DistributedFort(DistributedBattleAvatar.DistributedBattleAvatar):
         DistributedBattleAvatar.DistributedBattleAvatar.loadModel(self)
     
     def createGameFSM(self):
-        self.gameFSM = BattleAvatarGameFSM.BattleAvatarGameFSM(self)
+        self.gameFSM = FortGameFSM(self)
 
     def announceGenerate(self):
         self.notify.debug('announceGenerate')
